        "original_id": "18b7eeaf-5c04-5114-822d-2e05bcc11acb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lantana, Silybum, milk thistle\n- Animals: Strymon bazochii\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, biological control, invasive species management\n- Places: Hawaii\n\nFacts:\n- Lantana is a genus of about 150 species of perennial flowering plants in the verbena family Verbenaceae.\n- Silybum, also called milk thistle, is a genus of two species of thistles in the daisy family.\n- In 1902, Strymon bazochii was introduced to Hawaii to control Lantana species.\n- Strymon bazochii has proven unsuccessful at controlling Lantana species in Hawaii.",
